## 6. NSE — Nmap Scripting Engine

NSE allows Nmap to perform additional enumeration and security checks using scripts.

### Basic NSE

```bash
nmap -sC <TARGET>
```

Run default NSE scripts.

```bash
nmap --script <SCRIPT> <TARGET>
```

Run a specific script.

```bash
nmap --script <SCRIPT1>,<SCRIPT2> <TARGET>
```

Run multiple scripts.

### Useful Categories

| Category    | Purpose                           |
| ----------- | --------------------------------- |
| `default`   | Standard enumeration              |
| `discovery` | Discover additional information   |
| `safe`      | Generally safe checks             |
| `version`   | Service/version-related detection |
| `auth`      | Authentication-related checks     |
| `brute`     | Brute-force scripts               |
| `vuln`      | Vulnerability checks              |

Example:

```bash
sudo nmap --script vuln -p<PORTS> <TARGET>
```

> `dos`, `exploit`, `fuzzer`, and `intrusive` scripts may be disruptive.

---

## 7. HTTP Enumeration

```bash
sudo nmap -Pn -p80 --script http-enum <TARGET>
```

Enumerate common web resources.

```bash
sudo nmap -Pn -p80 --script http-title <TARGET>
```

Retrieve the HTTP page title.

```bash
sudo nmap -Pn -p80 --script http-headers <TARGET>
```

Retrieve HTTP headers.

```bash
sudo nmap -Pn -p80 --script "http-*" <TARGET>
```

Run HTTP-related NSE scripts.

---

## 8. Banner Grabbing

```bash
nmap -sV <TARGET>
```

Attempt service/version detection.

```bash
nmap --script banner <TARGET>
```

Use the banner NSE script.

```bash
nc -nv <TARGET> <PORT>
```

Manually connect to a service.

```bash
ncat -nv <TARGET> <PORT>
```

Ncat equivalent.

Example:

```bash
nc -nv 10.10.10.10 22
```

Possible result:

```text
SSH-2.0-OpenSSH_8.2p1 Ubuntu
```

---

## 9. OS Detection

```bash
sudo nmap -O <TARGET>
```

Attempt operating-system detection.

```bash
sudo nmap -O -Pn <TARGET>
```

OS detection while skipping host discovery.

```bash
sudo nmap -A <TARGET>
```

Aggressive scan including OS detection.

> OS detection can be ambiguous. Confirm with service banners when possible.

