## 15. Packet Tracing

```bash
sudo nmap --packet-trace <TARGET>
```

Display packets sent and received by Nmap.

Useful for understanding:

```text
SYN
SYN/ACK
RST
ICMP
```

Example:

```bash
sudo nmap -Pn --packet-trace -p80 <TARGET>
```

---

## 16. DNS Resolution

```bash
nmap -n <TARGET>
```

Disable DNS resolution.

Useful for faster and cleaner scans.

---

## 17. Saving Nmap Results

### Normal

```bash
sudo nmap -oN scan.nmap <TARGET>
```

### Grepable

```bash
sudo nmap -oG scan.gnmap <TARGET>
```

### XML

```bash
sudo nmap -oX scan.xml <TARGET>
```

### All major formats

```bash
sudo nmap -oA scan <TARGET>
```

Creates:

```text
scan.nmap
scan.gnmap
scan.xml
```

---

## 18. XML → HTML

```bash
xsltproc scan.xml -o scan.html
```

Convert Nmap XML output into an HTML report.

